    "withinDb": 1.5,
    "hardLimitDb": 3,
    "metric": "EBU R128 integrated loudness of the cue cut out of the decoded file (offset, duration as the game plays it) and padded with 1 s of silence; a v2 stand-in is measured with its play-time P1 trim added (src/audio/sfxV2/parityTrims.ts). Overall RMS and the true peak are recorded too; RMS follows the length of the tail and is not the rule."
  },
  "method": "A row inside the rule keeps its level. A row outside moves toward live's level to 1.0 dB from it (0.35 dB of margin is kept: a row within 0.15 dB of the edge is nudged in, the meter prints one decimal). A gain is applied to the lane's mastered file; when the gain would pass the mastering ceiling (-1.6 dBTP) the lane's own lookahead true-peak limiter (process.py tp_limit, 3 ms look-ahead, 80 ms release) holds it. The pack is rebuilt by tools/audio/sfx-parity-sprite.py (q3 core, q5 boss) from the lane's inputs with the re-levelled file in place of the lane's.",
